WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.200
Three Orbit devices in two NAT homes with a self-hosted orbit-net relay. Production binaries run in Linux network namespaces.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:22.100
A file written on the laptop reaches the desktop and the Pi in 4.0 seconds.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:38.700
The laptop's home router loses its internet link. The laptop and the desktop edit the same file.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:01:15.600
The link returns. 28 seconds later, all three devices report the concurrent edits as a conflict. Neither edit is lost.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:44.100
On the desktop, both versions are reviewed and one is selected. The other stays in history. The resolution reaches every device 3.4 seconds after confirmation.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:02:17.500
The Pi daemon is killed with SIGKILL while the laptop writes an 8 MiB file. After restarting, the Pi catches up in 8.5 seconds and the hashes match.
